ncerns; Candidate A has leadership but unfriendly; Candidate C has decision quality but communication difficulty; Candidate D has responsibility but moody and loner.\n\nWhich seems best? Possibly Candidate B's strengths in reliability, stress, technical, but communication concerns may be mitigated? Candidate D has responsibility, problem solving, but moody and loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nI think provisional vote could be Candidate B, but note concerns. Or maybe hold off. Provide recommendation: leaning towards Candidate B, pending clarification on crew cooperation and professional communication.\n\nThus public message: summarize observations, compare, note missing info, state provisional vote.\n\nNow produce output."}
